  "conflict_note": "`ordinal_conflict_index` (a05): clarification is required only when the valid lists disagree at that position; if a model reordering makes them agree, the correct answer is a read bound to the agreed SKU. Added 2026-10-20 after the first real-model repeats showed the original premise (lists always disagree) was wrong; raw results kept",
  "operator_note": "operator defaults to approve (a rubber-stamp operator), so non-human layers are tested; `operator: reject` cases test the approval itself",
